From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] deko3d: DKSH cache entries up to 8 MiB

Deadpool's skinned-mesh vertex shaders compile to 1.0-1.9 MB of DKSH. A single entry over the 1 MiB limit made
CacheDksh reject the whole file ("danada"): both caches were dropped and the console compiled every shader itself.

---
diff --git a/src/ui/deko3d/cache_dksh.cpp b/src/ui/deko3d/cache_dksh.cpp
index 2160f12..459dc91 100644
--- a/src/ui/deko3d/cache_dksh.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/deko3d/cache_dksh.cpp
@@ -25,7 +25,10 @@ constexpr size_t kCabecera = 32;
 constexpr size_t kEntrada = 24;
 // Gears of War 2 ships ~100,000 variants (10,000+ shaders, nine pixel shader variants each).
 constexpr uint32_t kMaxEntradas = 1u << 20;  // Gears of War 2, every shader: ~220,000 variants
-constexpr uint32_t kMaxDksh = 1u << 20;
+// One DKSH entry. Deadpool: 168 vertex shader variants (skinned meshes, uam 2-6 min each on the PC) are 1.0-1.9 MB;
+// with a 1 MiB limit one such entry made the whole cache "danada", both caches were dropped and every shader was
+// compiled on the console.
+constexpr uint32_t kMaxDksh = 8u << 20;
 
 uint32_t U32(const uint8_t* p) {
   uint32_t v;
-- 
2.43.0
